#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:2
msgid "FTC Docs Contributor Glossary"
msgstr "FTC Docs コントリビューター用語集"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:19
msgid "Branch"
msgstr "Branch"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:21
msgid ""
"A branch is a parallel version of a repository. It is contained within "
"the repository, but does not affect the primary or master branch, "
"allowing you to work freely without disrupting the \"live\" version. When"
" you've made the changes you want to make, you can merge your branch back"
" into the master branch to publish your changes."
msgstr ""
"Branch はリポジトリの並行バージョンです。リポジトリ内に含まれていますが、プライマリまたは master branch に"
"影響を与えないため、「本番」バージョンを乱すことなく自由に作業できます。"
"変更が完了したら、branch を master branch にマージして変更内容を公開できます。"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:32
msgid "Feature Branch"
msgstr "Feature Branch"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:34
msgid ""
"A feature branch is a branch that is created to work on a new feature or "
"bug. When you create a feature branch, you are making a copy of the main "
"branch and working on the feature in isolation. Once the feature is "
"complete, you can merge the feature branch back into the main branch."
msgstr ""
"Feature branch は新しい機能やバグに取り組むために作成される branch です。"
"feature branch を作成すると、main branch のコピーを作り、その機能を独立した環境で作業します。"
"機能が完成したら、feature branch を main branch にマージできます。"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:11
msgid "Fork"
msgstr "Fork"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:13
msgid ""
"A fork is a copy of a repository. Forking a repository allows you to "
"freely experiment with changes without affecting the original project. "
"Most commonly, forks are used to either propose changes to someone else's"
" project or to use someone else's project as a starting point for your "
"own idea."
msgstr ""
"Fork はリポジトリのコピーです。リポジトリを fork することで、元のプロジェクトに影響を与えることなく"
"自由に変更を試すことができます。fork は主に、他の人のプロジェクトへの変更を提案したり、"
"他の人のプロジェクトを自分のアイデアの出発点として使ったりするために使用されます。"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:28
msgid "Main"
msgstr "Main"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:30
msgid ""
"Main or main branch refers to the default branch of a repository. This is"
" the branch that is checked out when you clone a repository. By "
"convention, changes are made on feature branches and then merged into the"
" main branch when they are ready to be published."
msgstr ""
"Main または main branch はリポジトリのデフォルト branch を指します。"
"リポジトリをクローンした際にチェックアウトされる branch です。"
"慣習として、変更は feature branch 上で行われ、公開の準備ができたら main branch にマージされます。"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:23
msgid "Main Repository"
msgstr "Main Repository"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:25
msgid ""
"The main repository is the GitHub repository found at `github.com/FIRST-"
"Tech-Challenge/ftcdocs <https://github.com/FIRST-Tech-"
"Challenge/ftcdocs>`_. The files in this repository are the official "
"documentation for the FIRST Tech Challenge and the ones that are built "
"and deployed to the `FTC Docs website <https://ftc-"
"docs.firstinspires.org/en/latest/>`_. This should not be confused with "
"the main branch of a repository, which is the default branch of a "
"repository."
msgstr ""
"Main repository は `github.com/FIRST-Tech-Challenge/ftcdocs "
"<https://github.com/FIRST-Tech-Challenge/ftcdocs>`_ にある GitHub リポジトリです。"
"このリポジトリ内のファイルは FIRST Tech Challenge の公式ドキュメントであり、"
"`FTC Docs ウェブサイト <https://ftc-docs.firstinspires.org/en/latest/>`_ に"
"ビルド・デプロイされます。これはリポジトリのデフォルト branch であるリポジトリの "
"main branch と混同しないようにしてください。"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:6
msgid "Pull Request"
msgstr "Pull Request"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:8
msgid ""
"A pull request is a way to propose changes to a branch in a repository. "
"When you submit a pull request, you're requesting that the repository "
"owner pull in your changes. Pull requests show differences between the "
"content of the source branch and the target branch. The changes, "
"additions, and subtractions are shown in green, red, and grey, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""
"Pull request はリポジトリの branch への変更を提案する方法です。"
"pull request を送ると、リポジトリのオーナーに変更を取り込むよう依頼することになります。"
"pull request では、ソース branch とターゲット branch のコンテンツの差分が表示されます。"
"変更・追加・削除はそれぞれ緑・赤・グレーで表示されます。"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:15
msgid "Repository"
msgstr "Repository"

#: ../../source/contrib/tutorials/glossary/glossary.rst:17
msgid ""
"A repository is a central location in which data is stored and managed. "
"It can be a collection of files or directories, and it can be a place "
"where developers store their code, track changes, and collaborate with "
"others."
msgstr ""
"Repository はデータが保存・管理される中央の場所です。"
"ファイルやディレクトリの集合であり、開発者がコードを保存し、変更を追跡し、"
"他の人と共同作業を行う場所です。"

